{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 3 for unsigned x: u8\n  m = ceil(2^9 / 3) = 171 (0xab, 8 bits), shift s = 1\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^9)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*3 = 2^9 + e with e = 1 <= 2^1.  Write x = q*3 + r, 0 <= r < 3.  Then x*m/2^9 = x/3 + x*e/(3*2^9), and x*e/2^9 < 1 because |x| < 2^8, so the extra term is below 1/3: it cannot carry r/3 <= 2/3 past the next integer\n  m fits u8:\n    C:    q = (uint8_t)(((uint64_t)x * 0xab) >> 9);\n    in ucas: u8((u64(x) * 0xab) >> 9)\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u8, equals x / 3 for every x (256 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 8-bit arithmetic, equals x / 3 (C's truncating division) for every input (256 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 3 u8", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^9 / 3) = 171 (0xab, 8 bits), shift s = 1", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^9)", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*3 = 2^9 + e with e = 1 <= 2^1.  Write x = q*3 + r, 0 <= r < 3.  Then x*m/2^9 = x/3 + x*e/(3*2^9), and x*e/2^9 < 1 because |x| < 2^8, so the extra term is below 1/3: it cannot carry r/3 <= 2/3 past the next integer", "c": "   q = (uint8_t)(((uint64_t)x * 0xab) >> 9);", "in_ucas": "u8((u64(x) * 0xab) >> 9)", "headline": "x / 3 for unsigned x: u8", "details": ["m fits u8:"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u8, equals x / 3 for every x (256 inputs)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 8-bit arithmetic, equals x / 3 (C's truncating division) for every input (256 inputs)"}], "files": [], "text": "x / 3 for unsigned x: u8\n  m = ceil(2^9 / 3) = 171 (0xab, 8 bits), shift s = 1\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^9)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*3 = 2^9 + e with e = 1 <= 2^1.  Write x = q*3 + r, 0 <= r < 3.  Then x*m/2^9 = x/3 + x*e/(3*2^9), and x*e/2^9 < 1 because |x| < 2^8, so the extra term is below 1/3: it cannot carry r/3 <= 2/3 past the next integer\n  m fits u8:\n    C:    q = (uint8_t)(((uint64_t)x * 0xab) >> 9);\n    in ucas: u8((u64(x) * 0xab) >> 9)\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u8, equals x / 3 for every x (256 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 8-bit arithmetic, equals x / 3 (C's truncating division) for every input (256 inputs)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 7 for signed x: i32\n  m = ceil(2^34 / 7) = 2454267027 (0x92492493, 32 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^34 + e with e = 5 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  (for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)\n  as i32, m = -1840700269 (negative: the sequence adds x back):\n    C:    t = mulhs(x, -1840700269) + x; q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 7 i32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^34 / 7) = 2454267027 (0x92492493, 32 bits), shift s = 3", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*7 = 2^34 + e with e = 5 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer", "c": "   t = mulhs(x, -1840700269) + x; q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)", "headline": "x / 7 for signed x: i32", "details": ["(for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)", "as i32, m = -1840700269 (negative: the sequence adds x back):"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)"}], "files": [], "text": "x / 7 for signed x: i32\n  m = ceil(2^34 / 7) = 2454267027 (0x92492493, 32 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^34 + e with e = 5 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  (for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)\n  as i32, m = -1840700269 (negative: the sequence adds x back):\n    C:    t = mulhs(x, -1840700269) + x; q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 10 for signed x: i32\n  m = ceil(2^34 / 10) = 1717986919 (0x66666667, 31 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*10 = 2^34 + e with e = 6 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*10 + r, 0 <= r < 10.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/10 + x*e/(10*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/10: it cannot carry r/10 <= 9/10 past the next integer\n  (for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)\n  as i32, m = 1717986919:\n    C:    t = mulhs(x, 1717986919); q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 10 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 10 i32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^34 / 10) = 1717986919 (0x66666667, 31 bits), shift s = 3", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*10 = 2^34 + e with e = 6 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*10 + r, 0 <= r < 10.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/10 + x*e/(10*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/10: it cannot carry r/10 <= 9/10 past the next integer", "c": "   t = mulhs(x, 1717986919); q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)", "headline": "x / 10 for signed x: i32", "details": ["(for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)", "as i32, m = 1717986919:"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 10 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)"}], "files": [], "text": "x / 10 for signed x: i32\n  m = ceil(2^34 / 10) = 1717986919 (0x66666667, 31 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*10 = 2^34 + e with e = 6 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*10 + r, 0 <= r < 10.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/10 + x*e/(10*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/10: it cannot carry r/10 <= 9/10 past the next integer\n  (for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)\n  as i32, m = 1717986919:\n    C:    t = mulhs(x, 1717986919); q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 10 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}, "isError": false}}
